<p>I did mean testes, fixed it. thank you.</p>
<p>If I recall Bio 101 correctly (and that is a slim chance at best), all living things have an equivalent of a circulatory system. In that there is a method for moving water and nutrients into tissues that need it and moving waste products to where they can be eliminated. In plants, the equivalent would be the capalaries running from the roots throughout the plant. Even in single-celled amobea, there are mechanisms to push nutrients to the organelles that need them and push waste by-products out through the membrane.</p>

